From d017b74b6baf81d48403d8dcc18d42336a49979d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:58:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): each setup owns its WCS, Stock, Machine, Post,
 Fixtures and Tool list in the browser

The browser's Setup section shows one node per setup with a radio for
the active setup (ActivateSetup, undoable) and its own children: WCS,
Stock, Machine, Post, Fixtures (each fixture a child), Tool list and
Operations (1+n, machining order). A document without setups shows the
same children for its implicit setup. Clicking a node activates its
setup first, then opens its page, so no editor changes a setup the node
does not belong to.

A setup may own its machine and post (SetupDef.machine / .post, None =
follow the document's): new undoable SetSetupMachine / SetSetupPost, a
datum transfer carries the mount, project v55 (v54 files open
unchanged). The app mounts the active setup's machine and post; work
crossing mounts is refused by name (generating an op of a setup on other
steel, posting a program whose setups disagree). Tool list is the
document library filtered per setup (decision (b)).

The browser code moved out of panes.rs (browser_tree, browser_pane,
tree_menu), tree glyphs out of painted.rs; decisions in
docs/decisions/343-setup-tree.md. Follow-ups: #388, #389.

Fixes #343

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
